
You set the file name in your **VoucherPostingController.java** backend file, specifically inside the downloadFile endpoint.
Currently, it is hardcoded to exactly "Error_Report.xlsx". We just need to dynamically grab the current date and append it to that string.
Find the downloadFile method (around line 170 in your controller) and replace the entire method with this updated version:
```java
    /**
     * Downloads specific report types (ERROR or SUCCESS) with dynamic date appending.
     */
    @GetMapping("/download-bulk-file/{requestId}")
    public ResponseEntity<Resource> downloadFile(@PathVariable String requestId, @RequestParam String type) {
        byte[] data = voucherBulkValidationService.getFileBytes(requestId, type);
        if (data == null) {
            log.warn("DOWNLOAD_FAIL | File not found | ReqID: {} | Type: {}", requestId, type);
            return ResponseEntity.notFound().build();
        }

        // FIX: Grab the current date (e.g., "2026-06-18") and append it to the filename
        String currentDate = java.time.LocalDate.now().toString();
        String filename = type.equalsIgnoreCase("ERROR") 
                ? "Error_Report_" + currentDate + ".xlsx" 
                : "Success_" + currentDate + ".csv";

        MediaType mediaType = type.equalsIgnoreCase("ERROR")
                ? MediaType.parseMediaType("application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet")
                : MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN;

        return ResponseEntity.ok()
                .header(HttpHeaders.CONTENT_DISPOSITION, "attachment; filename=\"" + filename + "\"")
                .contentType(mediaType)
                .body(new ByteArrayResource(data));
    }

```
This will instantly change the downloaded file to look like **Error_Report_2026-06-18.xlsx**.
*(I also went ahead and added the date to the Success CSV file just in case, keeping everything perfectly uniform!)*
